WEBVTT

00:00.250 --> 00:05.679
Delivery Operations asks: of all parcels due by noon, how many arrived on time?

00:05.679 --> 00:11.476
At one in the afternoon, two arrived on time, one arrived late, and one is unfinished.

00:11.476 --> 00:15.261
The completed-delivery view shows sixty six point seven percent.

00:15.261 --> 00:17.281
Does that answer the meeting's question?

00:17.281 --> 00:19.408
Explain your denominator before continuing.

00:24.373 --> 00:28.740
The meeting needs all four parcels due, including the unfinished one.

00:28.740 --> 00:30.983
Two out of four gives fifty percent.

00:30.983 --> 00:34.089
Two out of three completed answers a different question.

00:34.089 --> 00:38.222
Refreshing the older report cannot change its completed-delivery definition.

00:38.222 --> 00:40.789
Search synonyms may help find a candidate, but

00:40.789 --> 00:42.694
they cannot make different definitions equivalent.

00:43.912 --> 00:47.166
Now inspect the page's illustrative quality review.

00:47.166 --> 00:50.910
The checked input has four rows and four distinct identifiers.

00:50.910 --> 00:54.104
All promised times are present; one empty completion

00:54.104 --> 00:56.489
time is allowed for the unfinished parcel.

00:56.489 --> 00:57.896
These checks pass.

00:57.896 --> 01:00.789
Is the all-due publication now ready for the meeting?

01:00.789 --> 01:03.512
Name the evidence still needed, then pause to think.

01:08.358 --> 01:13.094
Passed checks support uniqueness and required-value completeness for that input.

01:13.094 --> 01:17.688
They establish neither accurate timestamps nor delivery by the contract deadline.

01:17.688 --> 01:20.536
They do not prove that the calculation uses the all-due

01:20.536 --> 01:23.493
denominator, or that the report read its output.

01:23.493 --> 01:26.456
A contract records commitments; check results and

01:26.456 --> 01:28.903
delivery records show whether those commitments were met.

01:29.708 --> 01:31.366
Leave an actionable decision.

01:31.366 --> 01:35.570
Delivery Operations confirms the all-due rule and original customer promise.

01:35.570 --> 01:40.145
The reporting engineer verifies fifty percent, then attaches the published output

01:40.145 --> 01:42.664
identifier and report refresh evidence.

01:42.664 --> 01:44.905
The page's decision remains pending because

01:44.905 --> 01:47.365
no verified all-due publication is attached.

01:47.365 --> 01:51.498
Being discoverable or passing checks does not make a dataset suitable for every use.

01:52.417 --> 01:54.140
Try the page's map exercise.

01:54.140 --> 01:58.652
In Quality check's Example record, distinguish the rule's expected duplicate count

01:58.652 --> 02:00.941
from the observed four distinct identifiers.

02:00.941 --> 02:02.502
Then open Decision.

02:02.502 --> 02:06.242
Find the chosen rule, evidence gap, next action and owner.

02:06.242 --> 02:09.890
Explain why the meeting is not ready, then use Check your answer.

02:09.890 --> 02:12.974
The page keeps the full contract and change-review guidance.
